{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"title":"Choosing what to record","anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"],"title":"Testing","anchor":"Testing"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"Traffluent","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","title":"Traffluent","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An event is a value that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"SourceLocation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as one of the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"records","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"deliver(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: ","type":"text"},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"droppingCallSite()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Consent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ConsentCategory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. ","type":"text"},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, which satisfies its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Constraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"RejectionReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"rejectionReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"); a control’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreensAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which tracks ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which tracks ","type":"text"},{"code":"ControlActivated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). On every platform, ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackLifecycle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). A tracker given the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionEnded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). A tracker given ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sampler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SamplingDropReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and stamping each kept record with its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SampleRateKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The standard enrichers, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.application()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"operatingSystem()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"network()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" imports "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" macro derives an event’s conformances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and schema from its declaration, and every other module but "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own for apps that already use GRDB; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Traffluent","","@Event","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","title":"EventMacros","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances, name and schema from its struct declaration, and declare the constraints its properties satisfy."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"TrackerTesting","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked, in order.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","title":"SwiftUITracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Track a screen view each time a screen’s view controller appears, without a modifier or a call on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each screen.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}]},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","type":"topic","title":"TracingDestinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that adds each tracked event to the span that was active when it was tracked."}]},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"url":"\/documentation\/checksums","title":"Checksums","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The CRC-32 checksum of raw bytes, as zlib, PNG, gzip and Ethernet compute it."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","title":"CollectorEncoding","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" to send."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","title":"Persistence","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}]},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","title":"LifecycleTracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and make the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s records durable as the app leaves the foreground."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","title":"LoggingDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that writes each tracked event to a swift-log "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Logger"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","title":"UIKitTracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Sampling Events","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"url":"\/documentation\/events","title":"Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The types every other module shares: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinations","title":"Destinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where tracked events go: the "},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Identifying People","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","kind":"symbol","title":"Traffluent","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Consent Gating","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PrivacyManifests":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Privacy Manifests","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","type":"topic","title":"Automatic Tracking","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","title":"AutomaticControlTracking","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track a control activation each time a touch activates a UIKit control, without a call on each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"control."}]},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","title":"GRDBPersistence","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChoosingDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations"},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Put every event a tracker tracks in a session, and sample whole sessions."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/sessions","title":"Sessions"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","title":"Changing an Event","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Persisting Records","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","abstract":[{"text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trackers","kind":"symbol","title":"Trackers","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker app code tracks events with, and what it applies to each event before it is delivered: enrichers, samplers and consent."}]},"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson","kind":"symbol","title":"PropertyJSON","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[]},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","title":"StandardContext","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale and network connection it was tracked on."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"AppKitTracking","url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Let AppKit views find their tracker up the responder chain, and track what controls do."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Defining Events","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","kind":"article","title":"Tracking Events","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations."}]},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","title":"TrackingPlans","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks as a tracking plan, and check the events against the plan committed before them."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding","title":"PostHogEncoding","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Write batches of records for PostHog’s batch capture API, for an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to send.","type":"text"}]}}}